UNIQ(1)

NAME
     uniq - collapse repeated lines that sit next to each other

SYNOPSIS
     uniq [-cdu] [file]

DESCRIPTION
     Where the same line appears several times in a row, prints it
     once. It only compares neighbours, so sort the input first.

     -c     put in front of each line how many times it appeared
     -d     print only the lines that were repeated
     -u     print only the lines that were not

EXAMPLES
     cut -f1 /usr/adm/usage.log | sort | uniq -c

SEE ALSO
     sort(1)
